<p>No accompanied listening for this one. It's really rooted in my own Sikh beliefs here; of life after death, stories of swans diving into lakes and emerging &quot;pure,&quot; of people dying and leaving behind only fresh flowers. Partition hit my own grandfather hard; the rivers divided, that sort of thing. It's also a bit of a personal way to deal with some things going on.</p>
